  "HDFS-17342": {
    "jira_id": "HDFS-17342",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Fix DataNode may invalidates normal block causing missing block",
    "description": "When users read an append file, occasional exceptions may occur, such as org.apache.hadoop.hdfs.BlockMissingException: Could not obtain block: xxx.\r\n\r\nThis can happen if one thread is reading the block while writer thread is finalizing it simultaneously.\r\n\r\n*Root cause:*\r\n# The reader thread obtains a RBW replica from VolumeMap, such as: blk_xxx_xxx[RBW] and  the data file should be in /XXX/rbw/blk_xxx.\r\n# Simultaneously, the writer thread will finalize this block, moving it from the RBW directory to the FINALIZE directory. the data file is move from /XXX/rbw/block_xxx to /XXX/finalize/block_xxx.\r\n# The reader thread attempts to open this data input stream but encounters a FileNotFoundException because the data file /XXX/rbw/blk_xxx or meta file /XXX/rbw/blk_xxx_xxx doesn't exist at this moment.\r\n# The reader thread  will treats this block as corrupt, removes the replica from the volume map, and the DataNode reports the deleted block to the NameNode.\r\n# The NameNode removes this replica for the block.\r\n# If the current file replication is 1, this file will cause a missing block issue until this DataNode executes the DirectoryScanner again.\r\n\r\nAs described above, when the reader thread encountered FileNotFoundException is as expected, because the file is moved.\r\nSo we need to add a double check to the invalidateMissingBlock logic to verify whether the data file or meta file exists to avoid similar cases.\r\n",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "d023cff9ce127a4a7f29696c84c17f735520558f",
        "message": "HDFS-17342. Fix DataNode may invalidates normal block causing missing block",
        "author": "haiyang1987",
        "date": "2024-01-18T08:13:51Z",
        "files": [
          {
            "PARENT_PATH": "hadoop-hdfs-project/hadoop-hdfs/src/main/java/org/apache/hadoop/hdfs/server/datanode/DataNodeFaultInjector.java",
            "CHILD_PATH": "hadoop-hdfs-project/hadoop-hdfs/src/main/java/org/apache/hadoop/hdfs/server/datanode/DataNodeFaultInjector.java",
            "PATH_CHANGED": false,
            "LINES_ADDED": 5,
            "LINES_DELETED": 0,
            "PARENT_LOC": 170,
            "STATUS": "M"
